<header><h1>Sustain Damage: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_sustain_damage">Sustain Damage</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A ship in the active system may use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability to cancel a hit produced by a <a href="/R_space_cannon">space cannon</a> roll during the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87.4: &ldquo;A unit can use its &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability any time a hit is produced against it. This includes hits produced during combat and from unit abilities such as the &lsquo;Space Cannon&rsquo; ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a ship use Sustain Damage against Space Cannon hits?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; Sustain Damage can cancel any hit produced against the unit, Space Cannon included.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A mech committed to a planet may use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability to cancel a hit produced during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step by a unit on that planet.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87.4: Sustain Damage applies to &ldquo;unit abilities such as the &lsquo;Space Cannon&rsquo; ability.&rdquo; LRR 77.8: &ldquo;The active player must choose and destroy one of their ground forces on the planet for each hit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Mechs may use their <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability to cancel a hit produced by a <a href="/R_bombardment">bombardment</a> roll.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a ship use Sustain Damage against Space Cannon hits?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; Sustain Damage can cancel any hit produced against the unit.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87.4: &ldquo;A unit can use its &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability any time a hit is produced against it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A non&ndash;fighter ship cannot use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability to cancel a hit produced by an <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage">anti&ndash;fighter barrage</a> roll, unless an effect such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Waylay"><i>Waylay</i></a> action card makes it eligible to be hit.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87.4a: &ldquo;A unit can only use the &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability if it is eligible to be hit. For example, a player cannot use a dreadnought&rsquo;s &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability to cancel a hit from &lsquo;Anti-Fighter Barrage.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do Raid Formation and Waylay interact?&rdquo;: &ldquo;With Waylay, those hits still hit ships and the opponent assigns them normally, using Sustain Damage on undamaged ships if they like.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A unit may only use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability once in each timing window, even if it is repaired.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a ship repaired by the Empyrean flagship use Sustain Damage again in the same round?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; a unit can sustain only once per instance of the timing window.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the same unit could not use its Sustain Damage ability multiple times during the same timing window.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If multiple ships use their <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability, a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card may be played for each.<sup>1,2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Direct Hit&rsquo; can be used to follow up hits that are assigned by &lsquo;Ambush,&rsquo; &lsquo;Dimensional Splicer,&rsquo; &lsquo;Devotion,&rsquo; and other similar abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can several Direct Hits or Shields Holdings be played in the same combat round?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Several Direct Hits, yes: each Sustain Damage use is its own trigger, so you can answer each with a Direct Hit on that ship.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Because the Direct Hits are targeting different ships/instances of sustain damage use, this is allowed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>When a player uses the <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability of one of their ships, they do not have to decide if another of their ships in the same combat will use its <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability until after their opponent has used or declined to use a <i>Direct Hit</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can several Direct Hits or Shields Holdings be played in the same combat round?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Sustain Damage is used unit by unit, so you can wait to see a Direct Hit before sustaining with more.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A mech cannot be destroyed by <i>Direct Hit</i>, as it is not a ship.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Direct Hit destroy a mech that uses Sustain Damage?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; Direct Hit targets ships, and mechs are ground forces.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>All damaged units are repaired during the <a href="/R_status_phase">status phase</a>, even if a game effect has caused those units to no longer have the <sc>Sustain Damage</sc> ability.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87.3: &ldquo;A damaged unit cannot use the &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability until it is repaired during the status phase.&rdquo; Status phase repairs all damaged units.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
